#31012
NAME  mouse clockwork flicker brass~
SHORT a flickering clockwork mouse~
LONG  A small mouse of brass and glass skitters along the shelves, flickering.~
DESCR
The mouse is a clever little thing of brass gears and glass beads, made to run
the shelves and wind the smaller sand-clocks.  Something has gone wrong with it:
with every darting step it flickers, one instant bright and new, the next
rust-eaten and half-collapsed, then whole again.  Caught between its ages, it has
turned mean, and it bares needle teeth of splintered glass at anything that moves.
~
