LONG  A galvanic sentinel looms over the pedestal, wreathed in the arcs it was built to hold.~
DESCR
The last and largest of the engine's wardens, the sentinel is a great jointed
construct of blackened iron and coiled copper, raised to stand over the finished
work and let no hand near it.  Lightning runs the length of its frame in a slow,
deliberate crawl, held and shaped and never spent.  It does not pace.  It does
not sleep.  It only waits, humming, for something foolish enough to reach past it.
~
