#31023
NAME  guardian construct paradox warden~
SHORT a paradox-warden of dull silver~
LONG  A tall construct of dull silver stands watch, its many joints ticking a half-beat out of time with themselves.~
DESCR
The warden is built in the shape of a man and then corrected, over and over,
until it is the shape of nothing kind.  Plates of tarnished silver overlap its
frame, each stamped with a clock-face whose hands run backward.  It moves in
stutters, arriving where it means to be a moment before it sets out, so that the
eye can never quite hold it still.  It was made to keep a single room exactly as
it was, and it will kill anything that tries to make that room otherwise.
~
