#31027
NAME  unmade moment paradox guardian~
SHORT the unmade moment~
LONG  The unmade moment coils around the last certainty, guarding what he chose.~
DESCR
It has no shape you can hold in your eye for long -- a knot of the grey
unmaking itself, wearing for a heartbeat the face of a burning house, then a
rising river, then nothing at all.  This is the paradox given just enough will
to guard its own solution.  It does not want the last piece lifted from its
plinth.  It comes apart and together again with a sound like a caught breath,
and then it comes for you.
~
