No larger than a seed and brighter than a lamp, the mote simply holds wherever it
is set, perfectly still while the world ages around it.  This is the first of
Midian's "final work" -- a sliver of time made to stand outside of time.  It is
shaped, you sense, to be set into something: a fitting, a socket, the seat of a
small silver box.~
