EDESC calendar dial moon phases~
The calendar is a nest of engraved brass dials that turn of their own accord,
tracking the true moon in the sky far outside.  An inner ring names the eight
phases; an outer ring, in Midian's hand, carries a single instruction: "To climb
the Axis, leave each firmament only by the room whose moon matches the moon of
tonight.  The heavens do not forgive the wrong door -- they simply send you down
again."  A glance at the dial tells you which phase holds sway right now.~
End

#31012
