plainly old.  Beside where it lay rests its ruined twin: the same key eaten to
brown lace by rust, crumbling at a touch.  This one was that one, once.  Midian
ran it backward through his engine until every year of corrosion fell away, and
it shines now as it did the day it was cut.  It fits, surely, some lock this wing
was built around.~
End

