should rest, and never closing that gap.  It does not drift, does not settle --
for it, the fall has simply stopped.  This is a piece of Midian's final work, cut
and balanced with impossible care, its underside shaped to a small facet meant to
seat into the socket of a little silver box.  Held in the hand it weighs nothing
at all, as though it is only half here.~
