LEVEL  0
WEIGHT 1
COST   0
COND   100
EDESC letter friend second pebble~
The same warm, hurried hand, pressed harder this time.

  "The seed you sent came as a staff of dark wood -- aged forty years in a
  night, you wrote, and I do not doubt it, though my wife will not keep it in the
  house.  Midian, I marvel and I am afraid in the same breath.  You move stones
  and seeds and rusted keys through their years as easily as I turn a page.  But
  I hear the next question already behind your teeth, and I beg you: an object
  does not grieve if the moving goes wrong.  A man would.  Do not make yourself
  the proof.  I will come when you have gone slower, not sooner.  -- your friend"~
End

