#31010
NAME   The smooth wall of the cavern~
DESCR
The rough cavern stone ends abruptly here against a wall unlike the rest --
smooth, almost polished, curving away in a line far too regular to be natural.
Where the raw rock meets it the seam is seamless, as though the mountain had
been poured against a mould and left to set.  Something made this.
~
