#31011
NAME   The Edge Of The Collapsed Landslide~
DESCR
Broken earth and shattered stone sprawl across the mountainside here, where a
whole shoulder of the slope has torn loose and slid.  Uprooted saplings lie half
buried in the rubble, their roots clawing at the sky.  The scar is fresh -- no
moss, no weathering -- and picking your way across the loose scree is slow work.
~
