#31012
NAME   The Edge Of The Collapsed Landslide~
DESCR
The landslide narrows to a tongue of debris here, funneled between two stubborn
outcrops that refused to give way.  Dust still sifts down now and then from
above, hissing softly against the rubble.  A tumble of larger boulders blocks
the way north, though the gaps between them look as if they might be worked open.
~
