#31015
NAME   A Large Boulder~
DESCR
As you follow the western edge of the landslide you come to a gigantic boulder that seems to have fallen.  It's massive girth extends into the forest line to the south, leaving no obvious path to continue this direction.
~
FLAGS  0
Sect   5
DOOR 1
You see nothing special here.
~
~
0 0 31000
EDESC boulder rock~
Up close the boulder is the size of a small house, streaked with lichen and
scarred pale where it struck the slope on its long way down.  It is far too vast
and too deeply settled to move.  There is no path around it to the south -- only
forest, and stone, and the long walk back the way you came.~
EDESC claw marks scratches~
Low on the boulder's southern face, half hidden under a beard of moss, is a
cluster of old claw marks gouged into the rock -- some animal's, by the spacing,
though a large one.  They are weathered smooth and long abandoned.~
EDESC den burrow hole~
A dark gap opens under one edge of the boulder where the earth has washed away,
just wide enough for a fox or a badger.  A faint whiff of musk drifts out of it,
but whatever denned here is long gone, and the burrow is cold and empty.~
End

#31016
NAME   A small animal trail on the mountain~
DESCR
The trail switches back on itself here, hugging a bulge of grey stone.  Tufts of
hardy grass and pale mountain flowers cling to every crack that will hold a
little soil.  From this height the land below spreads out in folds of forest and
field, hazed blue with distance.
~
