0 0 31023
EDESC sky stars constellations moon night~
By day the sky here is a vast, clean blue, stitched to the grey mountains along
its northern rim.  But it is at night that this high field truly opens: with no
town for a hundred miles to dim them, the stars come out in their thousands,
wheeling in slow and ancient patterns.  You could learn to read the seasons in
them -- the hunter, the loom, the great slow turning of the moon -- if only you
had someone to teach you.  Someone, clearly, once tried.~
End

