#31059
NAME   The Rotting Apple Tree~
DESCR
This apple tree stump is surrounded by branches of a once great tree, now laid
low.  It's branches would have been at least a hundred feet high.  Now the
branches are strewn about this glade, some so rotten that they've been overcome
with moss and fungus.  You see something odd and faded etched into the base of
the trunk.  The air around the fallen trunk shivers faintly, like heat over
summer stone, though the glade is cold.  For just a moment, at the edge of your
vision, the rotted wood seems whole and green again -- and then it is gone, and
only the ruin remains.  Whatever happened here, time itself has not entirely
healed over it.~
