The last of the maintained cobblestone gives out here, and the road turns rough
and broken underfoot.  Weeds push up thick between the surviving stones, and deep
ruts run where the rains have carried the surface away.  Behind you to the east
the road still remembers being cared for; ahead to the west, it plainly does not.
