#31071
NAME   Pendulus Sanctum~
DESCR
The air in this vaulted antechamber moves in slow, measured sweeps, as though
some vast pendulum you cannot see counts out the seconds of the room itself.
Brass rails and half-dismantled consoles line the walls, and everywhere the
patient tick of hidden escapements presses against your ears.  An archway to the
north breathes out the smell of oil and hot metal; to the south, a sealed door
waits for a key that has not yet been cut.  Midian has been at work here, bending
the flow of hours around him the way a smith bends a bar of iron.
~
