#31073
NAME   Lightning Sanctum~
DESCR
The brass steps give way to a floor of black slate veined with raw copper, and
the air here bites clean and sharp with the smell of ozone.  This was the second
of Midian's workshops -- the one he raised after the stars failed him, when he
stopped watching time and set out to measure it.  Racks of glass capacitors line
the walls, most cracked and lightless, a scattered few still ticking with a faint
blue charge.  Overhead, dead relays hang in ordered rows like a congregation of
little iron saints.  Somewhere in the dark a spark leaps, cracks, and dies.  A
low doorway leads north into the engine proper; the way south is a blank,
unfinished threshold.
~
