#31075
NAME   Predictive Sanctum~
DESCR
You stand at the threshold of the last wing Midian ever built, and it is
already leaving.  The walls here do not so much end as thin, their far corners
gone soft and grey, unravelling into a fog that eats the edges of things.
Charts of hours-yet-to-come paper the near wall, but where they run out of
certainty the ink simply stops and the paper with it.  A cold draught that has
no source pulls always northward, toward the deeper rooms, as though the future
itself were drawing breath.  To the south a sealed way waits, patient, for a
door that has not yet been opened.
~
