A low side-cell off the great shaft, its ceiling a sparse scatter of dim,
unfamiliar stars.  The moon here shows as a waning sliver, thin and guttering, and
something about the whole arrangement feels subtly wrong -- a sky copied down by
someone who was, in the end, only guessing.  The path through leads only deeper
into the firmament.
