The eastern end of the gallery, where the instruments give way to a second great
sealed blast door in the north wall -- the twin of the one at the far west end,
and just as shut.  This one, the notes scrawled beside it insist, is the way OUT,
for a day when there is something to come out from.  A short stair leads down and
east toward a domed side chamber where a larger machine waits in the dark.
