EDESC window glass north~
Through the tall window in the north wall you look into a sealed white chamber
beyond the reach of the sealed doors.  At its centre, under a dome of flawless
glass, a single mote of starlight hangs perfectly still upon a pedestal.  The
jointed armature folded against this side of the glass is plainly built to reach
in and lift it -- but the levers that would drive it hang dead, and no hand has
worked them in a very long time.~
End

#31098
NAME   The Celestial Axis - Summit~
DESCR
The central shaft opens out at its summit into a broad gallery beneath the full
moon, which hangs directly overhead, whole and blinding-bright.  From here the
entire observatory is laid out below you like a working model of the heavens.
The Control Gallery runs east and west, its consoles waiting under the light, and
beyond it, to the north, the sealed silver doors of the experiment chamber gleam.
~
