#31101
NAME   The Control Gallery - West Terminus~
DESCR
The western end of a long gallery of instruments curved beneath the open night.
Banks of brass consoles line the wall, their dials frozen mid-reading, their
ledgers open to columns of star-positions in Midian's neat early hand.  Set into
the north wall is a great sealed blast door -- a mirror-smooth disc of silver
metal without seam or handle, save a single keyhole set oddly at its centre, and
cold to the touch.  A dead-end passage runs west into confusion.
~
