A short landing between the control gallery and the great domed chamber to the
south.  The walls here are painted with a map of the whole sky, gone dim and
flaking with age, its inked lines still precise enough to navigate by.  Below,
through a broad archway, you can see the vast turning shape of the Grand Orrery
wheeling slowly in the dark.
