#31105
NAME   The Grand Orrery~
DESCR
A domed chamber given over entirely to a single colossal machine: the Grand
Orrery, a nested cage of silver orbits large enough to walk within, each ring
bearing a painted world that drifts in slow, perfect order.  At its heart, where
the sun-globe should sit, there is instead a control station of dials and cranked
wheels.  This is where the whole observatory was aimed and read -- and where, the
notes say, the first true measurement of bent time was taken.  The moon painted on
the dome above stands full and exact.
~
