#31106
NAME   The West Airlock~
DESCR
A narrow chamber of seamless silver metal, sealed at its western end by the
mirror-smooth blast door that opens -- when it opens at all -- onto the control
gallery beyond.  In this early, unbroken age of the observatory it stays locked,
though a keyhole at its centre suggests it was never truly meant to stay that way.
To the east, a second doorway leads deeper into the experiment chamber itself.
~
