#31107
NAME   The Stellar Experiment Chamber~
DESCR
This is the heart of it: a domed white chamber where Midian first proved that
time could be bent.  Everything here is pristine, untouched, the air itself
faintly humming.  Rails of silver arc across the ceiling, and in the centre, on a
slender pedestal beneath a dome of flawless glass, a single mote of light drifts
and turns -- a fragment of starlight held perfectly, impossibly still.  Great
windows in the south wall look back into the control gallery, and jointed
armatures reach down from above, built to work upon the pedestal without any hand
ever entering this sterile room.
~
