#31112
NAME   The Sand-Clock Alcove~
DESCR
A snug alcove, its every surface crowded with sand-clocks -- squat, wide-mouthed
glasses meant for measuring small and precise spans.  One great hourglass stands
apart on a velvet-draped table, its sand heaped in the upper bulb and refusing to
fall.  Something small and quick skitters among the shelves, there and gone,
flickering as it runs.  A passage leads back west.
~
