#31120
NAME   The Broken Clepsydra~
DESCR
A quiet side-room given over to a single great water-clock -- a clepsydra of
bronze basins and thin copper pipes, taller than you are.  Its water has long
since stilled, and a faint green patina has crept across the lower metal, the
first and only disorder you have found in all this wing.  A folded letter lies on
the rim of the lowest basin, its wax seal already broken.  The only way out is
east.
~
