#31111
NAME   The Gallery of Hourglasses~
DESCR
The hall widens into a formal gallery, hourglasses set out on plinths down its
centre like treasures in a museum.  Small brass plaques name each one and the
span it was made to keep.  Here Midian's early triumphs stand on display with an
open, boyish pride -- the first glasses he tuned not merely to measure time, but
to lean against it.  Ways open east and west, and the gallery runs on to the
north.
~
