#31113
NAME   The Hall of Slow Hours~
DESCR
The gallery narrows again into a solemn hall where the light itself seems to move
thickly, catching in the falling sand like honey.  Every hourglass here runs at
its own wrong pace -- some racing, some barely trickling, a few hanging almost
frozen at the waist.  A passage opens east, and the hall climbs on toward the
north, where a low, steady humming can be felt more than heard.
~
