The ruined twin has rusted almost to nothing, its wards eaten away, its bow
crumbling at the lightest touch.  It is what the bright key in the cradle would
be, had Midian not run it backward through the drums until its years fell off it.~
End

#31116
NAME   The Control Gallery - West Terminus~
DESCR
The western end of a long gallery of consoles, their dials and levers still
bright and true.  This is where Midian governed the whole wing -- every hourglass,
every engine, answerable to the switches beneath his hand.  Set into the north
wall is a heavy vault door of pale silver, seamless but for a single keyhole at
its heart.  The gallery runs east, and a passage returns south toward the engine.
~
