#31118
NAME   The Experiment Chamber - The Still Hour~
DESCR
The innermost room of the chamber, and the stillest place you have ever stood.
Here time does not merely run slow -- it does not run at all.  On a slender pillar
at the room's centre, beneath a bell of clear glass, rests a single grain of sand,
held a finger's breadth above the pillar's top: not falling, not drifting, not
ever going to fall.  A silver door leads south, out of the chamber; the loom-room
lies west.
~
