EDESC grain sand bell pillar~
Look as long as you like: the grain does not fall.  It hangs in the still air as
though the very next instant has been taken away from it -- the one instant in
which it would have dropped.  This, plainly, is a piece of the work Midian built
this whole wing to reach.~
End

#31130
NAME   The Ticking Threshold~
DESCR
You stand at the mouth of the workshop proper, where a hundred clocks tick
slightly out of step with one another.  The sound builds and scatters, builds
and scatters, so that no two moments here feel quite the same length.  Cabinets
of tools stand open along the walls, their drawers labelled in a cramped, hurried
hand.  Time itself seems thicker here, dragging at your heels as you move north
into the deeper rooms.
~
