#31144
NAME   The Pendulum Colonnade~
DESCR
A long colonnade stretches before you, each pillar hung with a swinging pendulum
of a different length.  They sweep in a slow, staggered rhythm, brass bobs
catching the lamplight as they pass, and the floor beneath them is scored with
pale arcs where their tips have brushed the stone for years.  Someone has tuned
them with obsessive care; the pattern they trace is almost, but not quite, a
song.  The workshop opens wider to the north.
~
