#31140
NAME   The Escapement Row~
DESCR
Past the geared door the chamber narrows into a workshop row lined with
escapements, the tiny hearts of clocks, laid out in careful ranks.  Each one
ticks at its own pace, and the massed sound is like rain on a tin roof.  At the
north end a second door waits, its keyhole cut in the shape of an escapement's
forked pallet.  Whoever built this passage meant it to be walked in order.
~
