#31153
NAME   Furnace Row~
DESCR
A row of squat iron furnaces lines both walls, their mouths gaping and their
grates choked with slag.  One still burns, roaring without fuel, and the floor
before it has warped into slow ripples of cooled metal.  The heat here is a
physical weight; each breath scours your throat.  A construct labours among the
furnaces, tending fires that no longer need tending.  The corridor lies west, and
a fiercer glare bleeds through an opening to the east.
~
