#31159
NAME   The Forge Floor~
DESCR
Beyond the blast door lies the experiment chamber proper, and the heat returns
tenfold.  The floor is a single sheet of forge-iron, scored with channels once
meant to run with liquid fire.  Anvils and quenching troughs stand abandoned, and
half-finished work lies where it was dropped -- brackets and rings of that
strange silvery metal, warped now by the very heat that shaped them.  The sealed
door lies west; the chamber opens further east.
~
