#31170
NAME   The Copper Threshold~
DESCR
Beyond the sanctum the walls turn to riveted copper plate, green with age and
scored by old burns where the charge has jumped the seams.  A steady, uneasy hum
lives in the metal, felt in the teeth more than heard.  Bundled cables sag from
the ceiling in loops, some of them still live -- now and again one twitches and
throws a white spark across the passage.  The way runs north into the heart of
the engine; a low arch opens east onto a flooded bay.
~
