#31181
NAME   The Ozone Corridor~
DESCR
The corridor narrows and the hum climbs to a needling whine.  Spark-gaps have
been set into the walls at even intervals -- paired brass knobs, a hair apart --
and every few seconds a blue thread of light snaps between one pair and vanishes,
leaving the air thick with ozone and the ghost of thunder.  The floor is painted
with a single straight guide-line, worn but exact, drawn to keep a careful walker
clear of the arcs.  It runs on north.
~
