#31171
NAME   The Logic Vestibule~
DESCR
Here the engine shows its plan.  A round chamber opens out, and set into its
three inner walls are three great gate-frames of iron and glass, each stamped
deep with a word: AND to the east, OR to the west, and -- north, above a sealed
and cradled door -- the mark of the whole.  A reading-stand stands at the centre,
and on it a brittle primer card waits for anyone who would work the gates.  The
northern door is dead and dark, a copper cradle empty at its heart, and it will
not so much as shiver until something is seated there.
~
