#31173
NAME   The Spark-Gap Cage~
DESCR
A cramped iron cage of a room, ringed floor to ceiling with spark-terminals that
were meant to hold a test-charge safely penned.  The penning has failed.  Current
crawls the bars in slow blue veins, and the air is a solid wall of ozone and
heat.  On a scorched shelf, behind the worst of the arcing, a single live
bit-token still sits in its clip -- the AND gate's kept answer, waiting to be
claimed.  The only door is back south.
~
