#31176
NAME   The Control Gallery, West Bank~
DESCR
Past the relay door the engine opens into its control gallery, a long room walled
in slate panels studded with dials, plug-boards, and the cranked wheels by which
the whole machine was once conducted.  Most of the gauges are dead; a few needles
still tremble, reading currents that have nowhere left to go.  A tall blast door
of dull grey metal seals the north wall, a socket at its centre shaped for a key
this gallery was built to make.  The gallery runs on east.
~
