#31177
NAME   The Control Gallery, East Bank~
DESCR
The east end of the gallery is given wholly to the Adder Console -- a broad slate
desk of numbered keys, seat-slots, and a small casting-tray, the machine that
turns an answer into a key.  A schematic is pinned open beside it, and in the
tray, still faintly glowing, lies a freshly cast circuit key: the engine has
already run its sum and cast the answer, waiting only to be taken.  A second blast
door, the marked way back from the chamber, seals the north wall.
