A slim chamber of seamless grey metal, sealed at its southern end by the blast
door that opens -- when its key is turned -- back onto the control gallery.  This
is the marked way IN.  The walls are scorched where charge has forced the seams,
and a low current still sighs through the plating.  To the east, an inner doorway
leads into the experiment chamber itself.
