#31185
NAME   The Instrument Annex~
DESCR
A cramped annex off the chamber, packed with the fine instruments Midian used to
read his one great moment: galvanometers, spark-chronometers, and rack on rack of
scorched brass dials, all of them now stopped or shivering uselessly.  A workbench
along one wall is strewn with half-built cells and the burnt stubs of his notes,
abandoned mid-word.  Loose charge licks along the ceiling.  The only way out is
back south into the chamber.
~
