NAME   The East Airlock~
DESCR
The eastern twin of the entry airlock: a slim chamber of grey metal ending in a
sealed blast door, the marked way OUT of the experiment chamber.  This door needs
no key from within -- it opens outward, onto the far bank of the control gallery.
Loose current crawls the plating and the smell of ozone is thick enough to taste.
A doorway west leads back into the crackling heart of the lab.
~
