#31192
NAME   The Mirror Hall~
DESCR
A long panelled hall lined floor to ceiling with mirrors, and every mirror is
empty.  It is the same hall -- the same dust, the same cold lamps, the same
wrong ordinariness -- and you are almost certain you have not been here before,
though the certainty is beginning to feel rehearsed.  The way runs north and
back south as it did.  But here, in the eastern wall, one mirror hangs a
finger's width proud of the others, and behind its silvered edge shows a thin
dark seam of somewhere else.
~
