#31193
NAME   The Mirror Hall~
DESCR
A long panelled hall lined floor to ceiling with mirrors, and every mirror is
empty.  It is the same hall.  It is exactly, insistently the same hall, and the
dust lies undisturbed even where your own feet should have crossed it a moment
ago.  You are almost certain you have not been here before.  The certainty is a
lie and some cold animal part of you knows it: north from here does not go
onward.  North from here goes back to where you started, and will keep going
back forever, unless you have already found the seam and left.
~
