#31194
NAME   A Seam in the Repetition~
DESCR
You step sideways out of the hall and into the gap behind it, a narrow wedge of
space that the loop forgot to smooth away.  Here the mirrors are seen from the
back, plain grey board and cheap nails, and the endless corridor is revealed for
the cheap and cruel trick it is.  The air stops tasting of brass.  To the west
lies the seam you came through; to the north, at last, a way that goes somewhere
new -- a spill of instrument-light from a gallery beyond.
~
