#31195
NAME   The Control Gallery, West End~
DESCR
The west end of a long gallery given over to the study of paradox.  Consoles of
black glass and brass march along the walls, each crowned with a ring of mirrors
angled to face another mirror, so that every reading is reflected into itself
and never resolves.  The needles on the dials tremble but never fall.  A dead
mirror on the western wall shows a version of this gallery in which someone is
still standing; the way east runs on down the gallery, and the seam lies south.
~
