NAME   The Control Gallery, East End~
DESCR
The gallery's eastern end, where the consoles give up their pretence of order.
Ribbons of printed figures have vomited out across the floor, all of them
repeating, and a bank of mirrors overhead has cracked into a hundred wedges that
each hold a different second of the room.  A heavy cold breathes down from the
north, off the sealed threshold of the experiment chamber.  The gallery runs
back west; a way climbs north.
~
