#31199
NAME   Experiment Chamber, West Entry~
DESCR
You pass through the blast door into the experiment chamber, and the held-breath
sound closes over you.  This is the antechamber of the lab proper, its far
corners lost in a haze where the air itself seems to be running the same short
loop of stillness over and over.  Broken apparatus lies where it fell and has
gone on lying, unrusting, unmoved.  The blast door is west; the loop deepens to
the east, toward a light that flickers at exactly the same interval, always.
~
