AB 0 31198
EDESC skeleton toller bones body~
Slumped against the broken apparatus is a skeleton gone to clean bone, one hand
fallen open in its lap.  It is Toller -- you know him by the scorched timekeeper's
coat still hung on the bones, and by the watch cupped in the curl of his fingers,
ticking yet.  He chased his oldest friend across every age of this place and died
still chasing, and Midian never once turned and knew his face.  Whatever he
carried out of the lightning, he carried it this far, and here at the last he
stopped.~
End

#31200
NAME   The Laboratory That Will Not End~
DESCR
The heart of the loop, and the worst room you have entered in this place.  It is
a modest laboratory -- a bench, a stool overturned, a lamp -- but it is happening
on a ring, a single half-second of catastrophe played without pause.  The lamp
falls and is upright.  A beaker shatters and is whole.  And at the centre of it
Corin dies, and does not die, and dies again, forever, his grief always fresh.
A locked mirror-door seals the southern wall, its keyhole cut in the exact shape
of an ending.  The way back is west; a mirror of this room lies north.
~
