#31210
NAME   The Fraying Threshold~
DESCR
The corridor beyond the sanctum is coming undone.  Long seams of nothing run
floor to ceiling, and through them you glimpse not another room but a grey
absence, a place where the world has been quietly rubbed away.  What remains
still holds the shape of a hall of prophecy -- shelves of sealed almanacs, a
floor inlaid with the wheeling of stars -- but half of it hangs suspended over
erasure, held up by habit alone.  The way north is whole enough to walk.
Behind you, south, the sanctum still faintly glows.
~
