#31211
NAME   The Corridor of Prediction Engines~
DESCR
Machines line both walls of this long room, and every one of them is a clock
that tells no hour.  Instead their faces show weather that has not come, faces
you have not met, doors you have not yet opened.  Most have frayed to silence,
their glass gone milky and their needles still, but a few tick out their small
prophecies yet, to an empty room that no longer listens.  A branching passage
opens north into a wider dark; smaller doors stand east and west.
~
