#31213
NAME   The Chair Where He Watched~
DESCR
A single high-backed chair sits alone at the centre of this small chamber,
turned to face a wall of dead screens.  This is where he sat, you understand at
once -- for hours, for years -- watching every road the future could take.  The
floor around the chair is worn pale by the same two feet returning and
returning.  On a stand at its arm lies a folded page.  Everything here is grief
worn smooth, and the walls have begun to dissolve at their upper edges, as
though even this memory is being let go.
~
