#31221
NAME   The Ward of Erased Days~
DESCR
This narrow ward was meant to store the days he had already spent predicting,
each sealed away in its own drawer.  Now most of the drawers open onto nothing
at all -- not empty, but absent, the wood and its contents unmade together.  A
few survive, and from one juts the corner of a letter in a hand you have come
to know.  The room ends where the erasure begins, a soft grey wall that is not
a wall, and that you feel, strongly, you must not touch.
~
