#31212
NAME   The Branching Orrery~
DESCR
The ceiling of this round room holds a vast orrery, but its spheres are not
worlds -- they are outcomes.  From a single fixed point at its heart, arms of
brass branch and branch again, and at the tip of each hangs a small pane of
glass showing a moment that might yet be.  Three of these panes have fallen
loose and rest now on the central plinth, close enough to lift: one lit with
fire, one dark with water, and one perfectly, terribly still.  Branches lead
east and west into the possibilities; the way on lies north.
~
