#31222
NAME   The Branch That Burns~
DESCR
You follow one arm of the orrery into a room drenched in false firelight.  The
prediction painted across its walls is vivid and moving: a cottage alight, a
woman's shape at the window, and Midian's own figure frozen at the threshold a
heartbeat too late.  It has the awful sharpness of a thing the machine wanted
him to believe.  But the longer you look the more it flickers, like a lie
repeated too often, and the dissolving edges of the room show plainly through
the flames.
~
