#31223
NAME   The Branch That Drowns~
DESCR
This arm of the orrery ends in a cold and streaming dark.  The future here runs
with water: a river risen in the night, a pale hand slipping beneath the
surface, Midian's boat always one stroke short.  It is convincing in the way a
nightmare is convincing, all weight and no truth, and it too begins to come
apart at the seams, the painted flood thinning to grey where the room itself is
being unmade around it.
~
