#31214
NAME   The Prophecy Engine~
DESCR
The largest of the prediction engines fills this room, a cathedral of brass and
frozen glass that once turned every scrap of the present into a hundred
futures.  It is dying now.  Whole banks of it have frayed to nothing, and what
remains grinds on with a slow, arthritic patience, printing the same answer
over and over onto a spool of paper that dissolves as fast as it is written.  A
seer's lens rests forgotten on the reading-desk.  North, the control gallery
waits.
~
