#31215
NAME   The Control Gallery, East Console~
DESCR
The eastern half of a long gallery of consoles, where Midian once steered the
great engine's gaze.  The instruments here are the last he built and the most
unravelled, their casings gone translucent, their readings bleeding away at the
corners.  A dead archway north gapes where the experiment chamber lets out, its
threshold rimmed with the same grey nothing that is eating this whole wing.
The gallery runs on west; the puzzle rooms lie south.
~
