#31216
NAME   The Control Gallery, West Console~
DESCR
The western consoles are quieter, and colder.  Here a single great door seals
the north wall -- a disc of dull, frayed metal with a keyhole at its heart, the
last barrier between the gallery and the chamber where Midian meant to end
himself.  The lock is a strange one: its wards are cut not to a shape but to a
certainty, and only the one true future, carried in hand, will turn it.  The
gallery opens east.
~
FLAGS  0
Sect   0
DOOR 0
The last blast door, dull and half-unmade, seals the way north; its keyhole is cut to fit a single fixed outcome.~
door blast~
