#31224
NAME   The Half-Erased Laboratory~
DESCR
A laboratory, or the ghost of one.  Benches and apparatus stand in careful rows
along the room's eastern side; on its western side there is simply nothing, a
clean grey emptiness where the same benches must once have stood before they
were unmade.  The boundary between the two runs down the middle of the floor
like a tideline, and the instruments closest to it are frayed to lace.  East
and west the room continues, into being and out of it.
~
