#31219
NAME   The Fixed Point~
DESCR
At the heart of the chamber, everything stops.  Here the fraying has drawn back
into a perfect, held stillness, as though this one point were being protected
from the unmaking that claims all the rest.  A low plinth stands at the centre,
and on it, catching what little light remains, lies the last of Midian's work
-- a small, certain thing, waiting.  The room is silent in the particular way
of a held breath.  A frayed archway leads east; the way you came lies west.
~
